    "Description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: openvswitch: defer tunnel netdev_put to RCU release (CVE-2026-31678)\n\n* kernel: pNFS: Fix use-after-free in pnfs_update_layout() (CVE-2026-63800)\n\n* kernel: nfsd: fix posix_acl leak on SETACL decode failure (CVE-2026-53397)\n\n* kernel: nfsd: release layout stid on setlease failure (CVE-2026-53399)\n\n* kernel: NFSv4/flexfiles: reject zero filehandle version count (CVE-2026-53392)\n\n* kernel: NFSv4/pNFS: reject zero-length r_addr in nfs4_decode_mp_ds_addr (CVE-2026-53391)\n\n* kernel: NFSv4: include MAY_WRITE in open permission mask for O_TRUNC (CVE-2026-64298)\n\n* kernel: nvmet-rdma: handle inline data with a nonzero offset (CVE-2026-72129)\n\n* kernel: nvme: add missing SRCU grace period in error path (CVE-2026-89972)\n\n* kernel: nvme/ioctl: check SUBMIT_IO with nvme_cmd_allowed() (CVE-2026-90227)\n\n* kernel: tcp: prevent collapsing skbs across boundary in rtx queue (CVE-2026-98549)\n\n* kernel: kernel: Denial of Service via race condition in TCP socket lookup (CVE-2026-99288)\n\n* kernel: kernel: Out-of-bounds write in nfsd via crafted SEQUENCE compound requests (CVE-2026-99362)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* lpfc abort handler crashes after HBA reset (JIRA:RHEL-155282)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
